" 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671745 1072 #uuid "5eb285d8-9be0-5d20-a475-af1d186bdad2" 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671745 1074 "The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=6\\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-3y=6.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=3y+6,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3y+6\\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\  y \\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix} 3y+6 \\\\  y \\end{bmatrix}=⟨3y+6,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671746 1080 "⟨3y+6,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671746 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671746 1083 #uuid "5f9f5b46-90ef-5f6c-b3c3-cb27660604fc" 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671747 1080 "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671747 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671747 1083 #uuid "65b9f15e-9dc2-57a7-8776-072fce7609ee" 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671748 1080 "⟨3y-4,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671748 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671748 1083 #uuid "663701ee-ea16-5abe-b654-a4259844c1de" 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671749 1080 "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671749 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671749 1083 #uuid "6a555149-af22-5d1d-8b70-3429357ed0ea" 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671750 1068 #edb/ref 17592186671761 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671750 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671750 1071 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671750 1072 #uuid "6c9995c5-1dc2-5c84-888e-84f7f28ad60c" 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671750 1074 "The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-4\\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+2y=-4.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-2y-4,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-2y-4\\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\  y \\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix} -2y-4 \\\\  y \\end{bmatrix}=⟨-2y-4,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671751 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671735 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671751 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671736 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671751 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671737 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671751 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671744 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671751 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671756 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671751 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671751 1077 "selection" 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671751 1078 #edb/ref 17592186671744 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671751 1079 #uuid "86591107-a127-5d2e-9347-404b6dcfa373" 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671752 1068 #edb/ref 17592186671751 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671752 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671752 1071 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671752 1072 #uuid "8c894149-7948-5b92-979d-5971289cdee0" 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671752 1074 "The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-12\\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+2y=-12.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-2y-12,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-2y-12\\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\  y \\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix} -2y-12 \\\\  y \\end{bmatrix}=⟨-2y-12,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671753 1068 #edb/ref 17592186671755 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671753 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671753 1071 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 9 & -6 \\\\ 4 & 12 & -8 \\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671753 1072 #uuid "8cc6b874-4ef9-5579-b3e1-061950bc9381" 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671753 1074 "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 9 & -6 \\\\ 4 & 12 & -8 \\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 12 & -8 \\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671754 1080 "⟨2-3y,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671754 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671754 1083 #uuid "8d3179a7-f1b9-52b0-8b9d-a8413d704af8" 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671755 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671731 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671755 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671738 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671755 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671740 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671755 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671747 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671755 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671749 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671755 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671755 1077 "selection" 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671755 1078 #edb/ref 17592186671740 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671755 1079 #uuid "9260ebac-0601-58c2-8fe2-3fe8f0a108e6" 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671756 1080 "⟨2y-3,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139538676 17592186045443 true] [17592186671756 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538676 17592